# OnboardAGVs — register multiple AGVs with the master in one call.
# Batch sibling of OnboardAGV.srv. Wraps VDA5050Master::onboard_agv_batch.
#
# **Partial success**: each entry is processed independently. If 1 of N
# fails the other N-1 are still onboarded. The response echoes which
# entries newly onboarded and which were rejected.
#
# **Idempotent per entry**: re-onboarding an already-onboarded
# {manufacturer, serial_number} is a no-op and is omitted from both
# `onboarded` and `failed`. The caller can derive the skipped subset:
#   skipped = request.agvs - onboarded - failed
#
# **When to use**: fleet bring-up from a roster, DM-driven reconciliation,
# or any client with >1 AGV to register at once. For one-shot operator
# calls use OnboardAGV.srv (single).

AGVOnboardSpec[] agvs
---
# Action-effect lists. Already-onboarded entries are not echoed — they
# did not change state.
AGVOnboardSpec[] onboarded
AGVOnboardSpec[] failed
